Overview
This program demonstrates the implementation of a generic queue data structure using a linked list in C++. The queue supports basic operations like push, pop, front, size, and empty, as well as a custom move_to_rear function that moves the front element to the rear. Additionally, the program includes a recursive linear search function to find the last occurrence of a target in a vector, and an insertion sort function for sorting elements in a vector.

Files
Queue.h: Header file that contains the declaration and implementation of the Queue class template, along with all necessary queue operations.
linear_search.cpp: Contains a recursive linear search function to find the last occurrence of a target value in a vector.
insertion_sort.h: Header file containing a template function for insertion sort.
main.cpp: The driver program that demonstrates usage of the queue, recursive search, and insertion sort functions.
Functionality
Queue Data Structure (Queue.h)

push(T value): Adds an element to the rear of the queue.
pop(): Removes the element at the front of the queue.
front(): Returns the element at the front of the queue without removing it.
size(): Returns the number of elements in the queue.
empty(): Checks if the queue is empty.
move_to_rear(): Moves the front element to the rear of the queue.
Recursive Linear Search (linear_search.cpp)

linear_search_last: Finds the last occurrence of a target element in a vector using recursion.
Insertion Sort (insertion_sort.h)

insertion_sort: Sorts elements in a vector using the insertion sort algorithm.
Instructions for Running the Program
1. Compile the Program
Use the following command to compile the program:

bash
Copy code
g++ main.cpp -o queue_program
2. Run the Program
Once compiled, run the executable:

bash
Copy code
./queue_program
3. Expected Output
The program will display:

The initial contents of the queue.
The queue contents after moving the front element to the rear once.
The result of the last occurrence search in the vector.
The sorted vector using insertion sort.

